## Restrict domain creation to administrators

Context: Domain creation must be reserved for Databricks App administrators
with CAN_MANAGE. Non-admin users must not see create-domain controls, while
Editors and Builders must retain the ability to save assigned domains.

Changes:

1. src/api/routers/internal/_permissions.py
   Added a request-aware guard that distinguishes a new domain from an existing-domain save and rejects non-admin creation.
2. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   Enforced the creation guard before persisting a domain to the registry.
3. src/front/templates/home.html
   Marked the Home New Domain action as admin-only.
4. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_domains.html
   Marked the Registry Create a New Domain action as admin-only.
5. src/front/static/home/js/home.js
   Marked the empty-state create action as admin-only and routed it through the canonical domain creation flow.
6. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   Preserved the empty-state button's inline-flex layout when visible to admins.
7. src/front/templates/partials/layout/help_modal.html
   Documented the Admin-only creation policy and the assigned-domain workflow for Editors and Builders.
8. docs/development.md
   Updated the role capability matrix to reserve domain creation for Admin.
9. tests/units/api/test_admin_only_domain_create.py
   Added create-versus-save authorization coverage.
10. tests/units/front/test_admin_only_domain_create.py
    Added contracts for all admin-only create controls and the canonical empty-state action.

